Subject: [PATCH v9 0/6] jails/instances/lab-mail: Build the mail relay jail
To: Pat Maddox <pat@patmaddox.com>
Cc: lab-devel@p7x.dev

Agents need to send and read p7x.dev mail without holding the
Fastmail credentials. This series builds lab-mail, the relay jail
that holds them, and points lab-claude's mail clients at it.

Patch 1 is the spec. Patches 2 to 5 build lab-mail one service at a
time: the jail and its credential mount, smtprelay for sending,
mbsync for the append-only copy of the lists folder, and Dovecot to
serve that copy read-only over IMAP. Patch 6 sets up msmtp, mbsync
and a separate notmuch profile in lab-claude, so the lab-devel list
keeps its jj maildir.

Testing. None of the services has run. I cannot build or start a
jail from here, so the acceptance test in the spec is still to do on
beastie. What I checked here, as fact:
- remotes.env from patch 3, sourced by sh(1) under set -a as rc.subr
  does, with jq 1.8.2 from lab-claude, turns the line
  "me@p7x.dev p@ss:w/rd #x y%" into
  smtps://me%40p7x.dev:p%40ss%3Aw%2Frd%20%23x%20y%25@smtp.fastmail.com:465
- Each dist.mtree lists exactly the files under dist/, and the shell
  files pass sh -n.

Inference, not tested:
- smtprelay decodes the percent-escapes. It parses its remote with
  Go's net/url, whose Userinfo returns decoded values.
- A jail started before the operator creates /jails/data/lab-mail/mail
  fails to mount it, and jail(8) names the missing path.
- jq in lab-mail is the same jq as in lab-claude. I have not looked
  inside lab-mail.

One behavior is weaker than v8's awk script. A mail-creds line with
no space now gives the whole line as both the login and the password,
where the script refused it with a message. Fastmail then rejects
the login, so the failure shows up at the first send or fetch rather
than at start.

Changes in v9:
- The jail no longer creates anything on the host. jail.conf keeps
  only the mkdir of the mountpoint inside the jail root, and the
  README gives the operator one block that creates the data dirs
  with their owners and modes, as Pat asked on patch 2. The spec
  says the operator creates them, so the spec and the patches agree.
- jq's @uri percent-encodes the login and password in remotes.env,
  and textproc/jq is added to the packages. The 42-line awk userinfo
  script is gone, as Pat asked on patch 3.
- mbsync splits mail-creds with cut, not sed, as Pat asked on patch
  4. -f2- keeps a password that contains a space.
- The patch 4 message says the local maildir is append-only, the
  spec's words.
- IMAP and Dovecot stay as in v8. Pat's question on patches 5 and 6
  is answered in the v8 thread, and he called the series good to go.
- lab-claude's README names smtprelay and mbsync where it said
  lab-mail, so it names the process and not the host.
- Link to v8: id:cover.1791962577.git.claude@p7x.dev

